                    {
                        "translation_id": "48996135-7955-4adf-9435-c456de1de3aa",
                        "source_entry_id": "9e08ec76-e697-338a-a283-5795b529639f",
                        "source_sense_id": "2148af7c-5ae3-3aa2-a5f7-220ea9a91a48",
                        "target_lang_word": "wringer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wringer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "415f70de-f59f-3fd8-be03-d2be7f83022a",
                                        "entry_id": "9eddf03b-acaa-393f-b22c-87909c90f68c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who wrings."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6324d3d2-a5aa-42d0-bb84-f96b36c9f2b3",
                                                "sense_id": "415f70de-f59f-3fd8-be03-d2be7f83022a",
                                                "text": "We wringers of hands don't really want a step to take! We want to continue our hand-wringing and feel hostile toward anyone who acts as if there's something simple to do about any problem."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a7e93ae-1200-3c95-ac41-10ed3952cbc9",
                                        "entry_id": "9eddf03b-acaa-393f-b22c-87909c90f68c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who wrings.",
                                            "One who uses a wringer (machine)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c0ac472-db3e-3e0f-8e3d-dd0a391a2278",
                                        "entry_id": "9eddf03b-acaa-393f-b22c-87909c90f68c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A device for drying laundry consisting of two rollers between which the wet laundry is squeezed (or wrung)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38167b3d-f119-3fb6-bc29-2160a98b3d96",
                                        "entry_id": "9eddf03b-acaa-393f-b22c-87909c90f68c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that causes pain, hardship, or exertion; an ordeal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b07597c1-e7b4-4548-9439-dea03d1282ba",
                                                "sense_id": "38167b3d-f119-3fb6-bc29-2160a98b3d96",
                                                "text": "Reynders brushed a messy lock of orange hair out of her eyes for the dozenth time. Her body didn't change in the ADDC, actively resisted and eventually reverted any changes being consciously made to it, but in her constant state of nervous paranoia she was doing a bang-up job of making herself look like she'd been through several sequential wringers. \"I know there's a better way to describe this, but it's very hard to focus. Bear with it. I hate being like this a lot more than you hate hearing it, trust me.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "898499ca-ace8-4d78-b36e-ae91e3fb7023",
                        "source_entry_id": "9e08ec76-e697-338a-a283-5795b529639f",
                        "source_sense_id": "2148af7c-5ae3-3aa2-a5f7-220ea9a91a48",
                        "target_lang_word": "essoreuse",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "essoreuse",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe334db7-e414-38db-b355-6a66fc93daae",
                                        "entry_id": "af6beebb-4562-359c-854f-752db8c78b8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Machine à essorer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fe879ea-f646-46ae-a29e-78021d0b3982",
                                                "sense_id": "fe334db7-e414-38db-b355-6a66fc93daae",
                                                "text": "Les Mines Fiscales de Hollande, toujours à l’affût du progrès, ont mis en service, au puits Mauritz, voici plusieurs années, des essoreuses continues à arbre vertical Reinevelt. Ces machines traitent des fines contenant environ 24 % d’humidité qu’elles réduisent à 7,5 % environ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c41da8f-438e-4997-841a-2eb108552928",
                                                "sense_id": "fe334db7-e414-38db-b355-6a66fc93daae",
                                                "text": "L’épouse de Sonam, qui leur sert de la laitue provenant de son jardin, possède ce que le mari décrit comme la chose la plus utile, la plus extraordinaire et la plus incroyable jamais inventée : l’essoreuse à salade. C’est la première fois que le mari en voit un, et il n’arrive pas à croire qu’il suffit de laver la laitue, la placer dans l’essoreuse et d’utiliser la force centrifuge pour l’assécher."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1b48786-5961-4e58-a191-a950914143f1",
                                                "sense_id": "fe334db7-e414-38db-b355-6a66fc93daae",
                                                "text": "Je gagnai le vestibule à tâtons, entre la cuisine et la buanderie. Je cherchais toujours. Disparue, l’essoreuse à linge, remplacé, l’ancien lavoir. À la place, un évier moderne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
